JSUB(1)                        ZOAU Command Syntax                       JSUB(1)

NAME

	jsub - Submit a dataset or file containing JCL.

SYNOPSIS

	jsub [-hvdf] <jclpath>

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-f
		Specifies the JCL path is a UNIX file.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Submit a UNIX file, dataset, or member containing JCL.

EXAMPLES

	Submit JCL located in PDS dataset member EXAMPLE.JCL(EXAMPLE):
		jsub "EXAMPLE.JCL(EXAMPLE)"

	Submit JCL located in sequential dataset EXAMPLE.MY.JCL:
		jsub "EXAMPLE.MY.JCL"

	Submit JCL located in UNIX file myjcl.txt in current directory:
		jsub -f myjcl.txt

	Submit JCL located in UNIX file myjcl.txt two directories up:
		jsub -f ../../myjcl.txt

	Submit JCL located at absolute UNIX path /u/myuser/jclfiles/myjcl.txt:
		jsub -f /u/myuser/jclfiles/myjcl.txt

	Submit JCL through stdin:
		cat myjcl.txt | jsub

EXIT VALUES

	0
		jsub successfully applied the command to the dataset.

	other
		Error occurred. See error messages for details.

